@[disk-format step]
Now create filesystems on the partitions you just made (the device names
below are examples; @[lsblk] shows yours). For the root filesystem, ext4 is
the safe choice; xfs and btrfs also work:
  @[mkfs.ext4 /dev/sda2]
  @[mkfs.xfs /dev/sda2]
  @[mkfs.btrfs /dev/sda2]

UEFI: a new EFI system partition gets FAT32 (don't format one you are
reusing from another OS):
  @[mkfs.vfat -F 32 /dev/sda1]

Swap partition, if you made one:
  @[mkswap /dev/sda3]

Type @[next] to go to the next step.
